nt><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUNO YASUSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SEIKO EPSON CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJII, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISHIKAWA, HIROYUKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUNO, YASUSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SEIKO EPSON CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUJII MASAHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ISHIKAWA HIROYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUNO YASUSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJII, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISHIKAWA, HIROYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUNO, YASUSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An ink-jet head for ejecting an ink droplet from an ink nozzle by the charging/discharging between a counter electrode and vibrating plates. The counter electrode comprises a main electrode (10) and an auxiliary electrode (101), which is provided on the ink-nozzle's side in common with the vibrating plates (51). Auxiliary charging between the auxiliary electrode (101) and the vibrating plates (51) is effected to vibrate a meniscus in the ink nozzle (11) without ejecting a useless droplet. Consequently, the ink is prevented from forming a film on the meniscus, and an increase of the viscosity of the ink due to evaporation of the ink solvent is prevented by diffusing the ink in the ink passage.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une tête d'impression à jet d'encre qui éjecte une gouttelette d'encre d'une buse à encre par chargement/déchargement entre une contre-électrode et des plaques vibrantes. La contre-électrode comprend une électrode principale (10), et une électrode auxiliaire (101) ménagé sur le côté de la buse à encre en compagnie des plaques vibrantes (51). Le chargement auxiliaire entre l'électrode auxiliaire (101) et les plaques vibrantes (51) s'effectue de manière à faire vibrer un mémisque dans la buse à encre (11) sans éjection intempestive d'une gouttelette. Ainsi, on empêche que l'encre ne forme un film sur le ménisque. On empêche également que la viscosité de l'encre n'augmente due à l'évaporation du solvant d'encre en diffusant l'encre dans le passage de l'encre.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>